.TH GIT-CLK 1 "2026-11-10" "git-clk" "Git Manual"
.SH NAME
git-clk \- manage and document git aliases in one place
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git clk alias
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git-clk
keeps your git aliases, and a description for each one, in a single tracked file,
.IR aliases.gitconfig ,
next to the
.B git-clk
script.
That file is a normal git config file, pulled into
.I ~/.gitconfig
by a single
.B include.path
line, so the aliases are version controlled and travel with the repository.
.PP
Descriptions live in a
.B [clkdoc]
section of the same file, which git ignores:
.PP
.RS
.nf
[alias]
	unstage = restore --staged
[clkdoc]
	unstage = Unstage paths, keeping the worktree changes
.fi
.RE
.PP
Alias lists are files in
.I aliases.d/<name>.gitconfig
in the same format; importing a list merges it into the managed file.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR "alias list " [ -v "] [" --markdown "] [" \fIpattern\fP ]
List managed aliases with their descriptions.
.B -v
also shows each expansion;
.B --markdown
prints a table suitable for READMEs or notes.
.I pattern
matches alias names and descriptions.
.TP
.BI "alias show " name
Show an alias, its description, and whether git actually uses it or it is shadowed by another config file.
.TP
.BR "alias add " [ -f "] [" -m
.IR desc ]
.I name expansion...
Add an alias.
.B -f
replaces an existing alias, or allows a name that is a built-in git command (which git would ignore).
.TP
.BI "alias rm " name...
Remove aliases and their descriptions.
.TP
.BI "alias doc " name " \fR[\fP" desc \fR]\fP
Set a description, or clear it when
.I desc
is omitted.
.TP
.BR "alias import " [ -f "] [" -n ]
.I list...
Merge alias lists (a list name or a file path) into the managed file.
Aliases that already exist with a different expansion are skipped unless
.B -f
is given;
.B -n
shows what would change without writing.
.TP
.BR "alias import " [ -f "] [" -n "] " --global " [" --move ]
Pull loose aliases out of
.IR ~/.gitconfig ;
.B --move
removes the imported ones from
.I ~/.gitconfig
afterwards.
.TP
.BI "alias export " "list name..."
Copy managed aliases and their descriptions into
.IR aliases.d/<list>.gitconfig .
.TP
.B alias lists
Show the available alias lists.
.TP
.B alias status
Show the managed file, whether it is installed, and any conflicts.
.TP
.BR "alias install" ", " "alias uninstall"
Add or remove the
.B include.path
line in
.IR ~/.gitconfig .
Both are idempotent.
.TP
.B alias edit
Open the managed file in
.BR $VISUAL " or " $EDITOR .
.TP
.B help
Print the command summary.
.SH EXAMPLES
Set up managed aliases from the bundled lists and install them:
.RS
.nf
$ git clk alias lists
$ git clk alias import log basics
$ git clk alias import --global --move
$ git clk alias install
.fi
.RE
.PP
Add a documented alias, including a shell alias:
.RS
.nf
$ git clk alias add last 'log -1 --stat' -m "Show the last commit"
$ git clk alias add who '!git config user.name' -m "Who am I"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Share a few aliases as a new list:
.RS
.nf
$ git clk alias export mine last who
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I aliases.gitconfig
Managed aliases, next to the
.B git-clk
script (resolved through symlinks).
.TP
.I aliases.d/*.gitconfig
Alias lists.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CLK_ALIAS_FILE
Use a different managed alias file.
.TP
.B CLK_ALIAS_LISTS
Use a different alias list directory.
.TP
.B GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL
Honoured as the location of the global config (default
.IR ~/.gitconfig ).
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Options can go anywhere; everything after
.B --
is taken as the expansion.
.IP \(bu 2
Shell aliases (starting with
.BR ! )
run under
.BR /bin/sh ,
so use POSIX syntax.
.IP \(bu 2
.B git clk --help
makes git look for this man page;
.B git clk help
prints the summary.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B git-clk
exits with status 0 on success, and non-zero on error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR git-config (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by cking.
